STEP 1 — DELTA
- [NEW] api.signageos.io versioned REST surface confirmed: `/v1/<resource>` and `/v2/device` return **403 auth-required** (not 404) on 19 routes — `device, organization, company, alert, alert/count, alert-rule, timing, location, emulator, package, policy, firmware/version, runner/version, plugin/version, content-guard/category, bulk-operation, organization-tag, device/telemetry/latest, v2/device`. Reverses prior "no public API surface" conclusion (which only probed bare `/v1`).
- [NEW] API auth model: `X-Auth` header, JWT expected — 403 body `{"errorCode":403105,"errorName":"WRONG_JWT_TOKEN","errorDetail":"Decoding of provided JWT token has failed"}`. SDK `requester.ts` also supports legacy `X-Auth: clientId:secret` and appends `organizationUid` as query param for JWT auth.
- [NEW] JWT source: Auth0 Device Authorization Flow (CLI `sos login`) against `auth0.signageos.io`, public clientId `8AU8D3zJ4mK8gszZP3gZO0nv9DusSNjV`, audience `https://sos-production.us.auth0.com/api/v2/` (from cli `predefinedRegions.ts`).
- [NEW] SDK resource map for `/v1`+`/v2` recovered by RAG (signageos/sdk `src/RestApi`): full list above plus `policy-status` (404 — route not exposed) and `v1`/`v2` version enum.
- [CHANGED] api.signageos.io auth model no longer "unknown" — now `X-Auth` JWT.
- [CHANGED] Prior LEARN "REJECTED IDOR @ api.signageos.io (no endpoints)" superseded: routes exist, auth-gated only.

